On-screen text is only a fact the narration states: a date, a clock time, a place, a distance, a count or a name. Never retype the sentence, and never invent a time, number or label.
Put a blackbeat directly before each detonation (Hiroshima 08:15 AM, Nagasaki 11:02 AM) and optionally directly after it, at most 4 in the film. Use rosetint only on the 2-4 most harrowing real shots (burned survivors, the flattened city).
